{"id":17026,"name":"Carroll County","slug":"carroll-county","state":"Maryland","code":"MD","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/maryland-tax-liens-earn-solid-as-a-beginner/carroll-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-13T12:29:53","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Lien Sale","redemptionPeriod":"Six months and one day from the date of sale","interestRate":"14% annually","bidProcedure":"Public auction to the highest bidder, no high bid premium","extra":[{"label":"Typical Date of Sale","value":"Last business day of June"},{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Carroll County Collections Office, Phone: 410-386-2971"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"RealAuction.com"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Carroll County Government"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"479LuMfSTWnSs2U0rEoQn0Bq7cPigGhRRhwdIdWEQtbFMj9pcO66v3ZKVLC5BDmw2HOeaC\"><iframe title=\"Win Big with 14% ROI - Carroll County - Maryland Tax Lien Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/quy-MxqLhhQ?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Earn 14% Annually at Carroll County&#8217;s Tax Lien Sale!</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Imagine locking in a 14% annual return on your investment at Carroll County, Maryland&#8217;s Tax Lien Sale! This can be an incredible opportunity if you know the ropes. Let&#8217;s break down the essentials.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"How-to-Get-Started\">How to Get Started</h3>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Register in Advance:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Register early on the auction site. Provide necessary details like your name, address, and tax ID. Compliance with Maryland’s business regulations is crucial.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"2\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Bidding Process:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Bidding starts with the Tax Collector’s minimum, covering taxes and fees. If you bid over four times the assessed property value, ensure you have a strong justification.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"3\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Payment:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Payments are processed via ACH Debit on sale day. Missing this step can result in losing your spot.The county will issue a Tax Sale Certificate within two weeks.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"4\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Interest and Foreclosure:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>You earn a 14% annual interest on your investment. Foreclosure opportunities open six months after the sale, with a two-year cap on redemption rights.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"5\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Conditions and Responsibilities:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The county sells properties &#8220;as-is&#8221; without guarantees on title marketability or property details. Clear all property charges before recording the deed. The county reimburses voided sales but deducts service charges.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Key Details:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Farm-field-and-dirt-road-in-rural-Carroll-County-Maryland-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17029 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Farm field and dirt road in rural Carroll County, Maryland\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Important Considerations</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Interest Rate</strong>: The county offers a 14% annual interest rate on tax lien certificates.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Voided Sales</strong>: If the county voids a sale, they will reimburse your bid amount, deducting the service charges.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Certificate Transfer</strong>: You can transfer certificates with proper documentation</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Foreclosure</strong>: You can initiate foreclosure six months after the sale, with a two-year limit on redemption rights.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Property Condition</strong>: The county sells properties &#8220;as-is.&#8221; Clear all charges before recording the deed.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Interesting Facts about Carroll County</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Location</strong>: Carroll County is in Maryland, with Westminster as its county seat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Population</strong>: As of the 2020 census, the population was 172,891.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Interesting-Facts-About-Carroll-County\">FAQs</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if the property owner redeems the lien?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: If the property owner redeems the lien within the redemption period, you&#8217;ll receive your investment back plus the 14% annual interest.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Can I transfer my Tax Sale Certificate?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: Yes, you can transfer certificates, but you must provide proper documentation, and the property owner cannot serve as the transferee.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What if the property doesn&#8217;t get redeemed?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: You can start foreclosure proceedings six months after the sale. Ensure you follow all legal requirements and consult with the Collections Office.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Useful-Links\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://carroll.marylandtaxsale.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Carroll County Tax Sale Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Carroll County Government Website</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://dat.maryland.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Maryland Department of Assessments and Taxation</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/government/directory/comptroller/collectionstaxes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Collections Office</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://realauction.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=